    "question": {
      "source_id": "unreconciled:step-q181685",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14116619/assets/f2d1c647ec7899221567d67e24e90a9f1efca60650b82a739e843e4085be636e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,2x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,-x+3}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=2x$ and *below* the line $y=-x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>2x,\\,y<-x+3.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n2x<y<-x+3.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x<y<-x+3}.\n$$",
